  "body": "Taken straight from #matrix-dev:matrix.org: https://matrix.to/#/!XqBunHwQIXUiqCaoxq:matrix.org/$14941627314087jmEbk:elynx.fr\r\n\r\n```\r\nHiro Lynx\r\nHeya. I have a friend that has a Matrix instance of which db is corrupted. The instance won’t synchronise some rooms, and it thinks that some users are in or out of rooms where other instances think otherwise.\r\nIs there an easy fix for such a situation?\r\n\r\nMax (@max:kamax.io)\r\nHiro Lynx (@Hiro:elynx.fr): how did it get corrupted exactly?\r\n\r\nHiro Lynx\r\nNot sure. He was using sqlite, had random segfaults due to ujson/musl incompatibility (on ARM processor) and OOM killing because not enough RAM.\r\nMostly not synapse fault IMO.\r\n(we replaced ujson with json to make Synapse work with musl. This patch is working fine on my system, although I have a x86_64 CPU)\r\n\r\nMatthew (@matthew:matrix.org)\r\nin theory it should self-heal, but you may have hit bugs\r\n\r\nwill need full logs\r\n\r\nKooda[b] (IRC)\r\nThis is what I see when trying to send messages to the problematic rooms: http://lxp.fr/p3EQ03eOwA\r\nWhen I try to leave it: http://lxp.fr/p3ER2eWuFQ\r\n```",
